  "whyItMatters": "Releases belong to member ends, the rotation belongs to the node. If every member end at a node is released, nothing holds the node's rotation: the stiffness matrix is singular. The structure may still look sensible (each member is pinned), but there is no solution; the correct answer is the diagnosis of the mechanism, and the fix is to keep one member end connected.",
